  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models clearly dominate (0.485–0.591) over image-only ResNet50 (0.208), and within RNA, multi-profile with avgpool aggregation (config_002, acc 0.591) is the best setting so far, outperforming both single-profile (0.485) and transformer aggregation (0.519). Uncertainty: PCA n2000 is the only RNA encoder tested; it is a linear dimensionality reduction and may leave substantial signal on the table. Question: Does replacing the linear PCA encoder with the learned scvi_n200 VAE encoder improve performance in the already-best RNA configuration (multi-profile, avgpool)? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002. Why this is the best next experiment: RNA is the dominant signal, so improving its representation is the highest-leverage design decision before committing budget to multimodal fusion. If scvi_n200 lifts accuracy meaningfully over PCA, it validates learned encoders and directly informs which RNA encoder to pair with image in later multimodal runs. If it does not help, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can focus budget on fusion/image questions. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about a core design axis."
}

